======================================================================================================================
SUMMARY
======================================================================================================================
  Does the dark fluid's conversion run away through the web?  Partly -- yes through the collapsed and turned-around web at
  z <~ 1.5, no through the voids, and not at z >~ 3.
  Nominal cell: the smooth (non-halo) carrier converts f_web = 1.00/1.00/1.00/1.00 at z = 3/2/1/0 (most conservative bracket
  1.00/1.00/1.00/1.00); with the halos, F_tot = 1.00/1.00/1.00/1.00 (halo only
  0.36/0.44/0.53/0.63).  The converted web is one connected set.
  What drives it: the halos' own daughters seed the multistream and turned-around web around them (momentum matching through
  the infall), and turned-around sheets ignite by themselves on the zero-strain cone.  What stops it: expanding flow (no
  re-resonance; the voids keep 0% of their carrier), and the gate at high z (rho_t/rho_bar = 36/68 at z = 3/4).
  Across the band: F_tot(0) 1.00-1.00, F_tot(1) 1.00-1.00; S8 ratio 0.923 (nominal).

  checks: 10/13 pass; load-bearing failures: 3   [529s]
exit code: 1
